# NEXT.JS 16.1.1 & REACT ARCHITECTURE
- STRICT ASYNC: Always `await` dynamic APIs (`params`, `searchParams`, `cookies`, `headers`) in Server Components/Actions.
- NO SSR FALSE: Never use `next/dynamic` with `{ ssr: false }` inside Server Components.
- OPTIMIZATION: Mandatory use of `next/image` and `next/font`.
- STATE: Use React Suspense with Skeleton loading for async operations.

# DOMAIN-DRIVEN DESIGN (DDD) & CLEAN CODE
- MODULARITY: Keep business logic inside `src/features/`. Do not bloat `src/app`.
- SOLID & SRP: Functions must be small, single-responsibility. 
- NESTING LIMIT: Maximum 2 levels of indentation per function. Early returns preferred.

# UI/UX & STYLING (TAILWIND CSS)
- DESIGN SYSTEM: Mobile-First approach (PWA ready).
- THEME: Slate/Zinc (Neutral) with Indigo/Deep Violet (Primary Accents).
- INTERACTIONS: All clickable elements MUST include `active:scale-95 transition-all duration-200`.
- GLASSMORPHISM: Use `bg-white/70 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/20` for floating cards/navs.
- FEEDBACK: Mandatory Skeleton Loaders during fetch, Toast Notifications for success/error states.

# SUPABASE & DATABASE SECURITY
- RLS STRICT: All queries must respect Row Level Security via `auth.uid()`.
- DATA ISOLATION: Cross-tenant/cross-user data leakage is strictly prohibited.
- AUTHENTICATION: Mandatory regex validation for emails: `/^[a-zA-Z0-9._%+-]+@[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+\.(ac\.id|edu)$/`.

# VALIDATION & TYPES (ZOD)
- STRICT TYPING: TypeScript strict mode enabled. No `any` types.
- ZOD EVERYWHERE: All API payloads, Server Actions inputs, and Form submissions MUST be validated with Zod schemas before processing.